 "description": "Ring-flag conservation across the discard step (pins deck_discard_banked; sibling battle_reshuffle_ring pins the fold and copy-back): a 6-card deck [SW SW SW SW R R] attacks with a sword (T1), defends with the pristine pile ring plus a sword (T2, ring blocks 0 under poker-hands-only scoring), then defends with both refill-redealt slots (T3). The T2 refill reshuffles the T2-played ring back into the hand, so T3's combo contains a discard-cycled ring. T4 is a single-sword defend that advances past the reshuffle-skip to the next attack turn; T5 stages the twice-cycled ring with a sword: with the flag intact the joker makes a PAIR of 5s that converts to healing (base 10 x 120% = HEALED amount 12, cause 1). If the discard step drops the flag, the cycled ring attacks as a flagless heal card for 4 unscaled damage instead (no cause-1 heal).",
